# Project: n8n-nodes-twitch-comprehensive

## Overview
- Community node for Twitch API with 70+ operations and triggers.
- Dual authentication: App Access Token (`twitchApi`) and User Access Token (`twitchOAuth2Api`).
- TypeScript strict mode, follows n8n community node conventions.

## Build & Dev
- Build: `npm run build` (tsc + gulp icons)
- Watch: `npm run dev`
- Lint: `npm run lint` / `npm run lintfix`
- Node >= 20, npm >= 10

## Auth Selection Rules
- EventSub: App token
- Streams Followed, Clips (POST), Commercials (POST), Schedule mutations, Stream markers, Chat, Users mutations: User token
- Analytics (extensions, games): User token with scopes
- Bits leaderboard, Extensions transactions: App token

## Scopes per Operation (partial)
- Get Extension Analytics: `analytics:read:extensions`
- Get Game Analytics: `analytics:read:games`

## Node Parameters
- Date parameters use RFC3339; for analytics, `started_at` and `ended_at` must be provided together.
- `after` is ignored for extension analytics when `extension_id` is set.
- `after` is ignored for game analytics when `game_id` is set.

## Additional Notes
- The node auto-selects user authentication for `/analytics/extensions` and `/analytics/games` and will throw if only one of `started_at`/`ended_at` is provided.

## Publishing
- Versioning: Semantic Versioning, no breaking changes in minor/patch.
- Prepublish builds via `prepublishOnly`.
